{"kind":"report","text":"Ready for independent review at exact clean head 1418d875ea1710a6f7f51613c07b3379642514a3 on request/undefined-kind-warning, artifact b2bbee486f27c45671ebf3fad0898cd97cd6f604.\n\nWHAT CHANGED. Vocabulary.UndefinedKindWarning in internal/workroom/kinds.go builds the warning from the live definitions, so no kind list is compiled in and a room that declares its own kinds, or binds its own fold, names the kinds it actually has. cmd/gs submitSigned calls it after the act lands, which covers gs state, gs review and gs batch, because every command that signs an act for an author passes through that one function; the warning goes to stderr. cmd/gitseq-mcp withKindWarning puts the same words in the state tool result, and summarize repeats them in the text block, so an agent that reads only the summary still sees it. It reaches the caller on both MCP paths: through the resident service and, when none answers, on the direct local append.\n\nWHAT DID NOT CHANGE. No refusal, no setting that makes it fatal, no list of allowed kinds. The kernel and the fold are untouched; the act lands, stays visible as an attempt, and still projects undefined-kind.\n\nTESTS, AND THAT THEY CAN FAIL. TestStateWithAnUndefinedKindStillLandsAndProjectsUndefinedKind proves the act lands and carries the undefined-kind verdict. TestStateWithAnUndefinedKindWarnsTheAuthorOnStandardError proves the warning reaches stderr, names the kind, says no rule reads it and that no lifecycle edge forms, lists every defined kind, and stays silent for a defined kind. TestStateToolCarriesTheUndefinedKindWarningInItsResult proves the same through MCP, in the structured result and the text block, with a resident service and without one. I broke each half and checked: removing the warning emission from both writing paths fails only the two warning tests and leaves the landing test green; turning the warning into a refusal before the submit fails the landing test. Both breaks were reverted from backups and the restored diff re-read.\n\nGATES at this head: make vet, make test and make race all pass, including the spike packages, which are in the root module now. gofmt reports nothing. The worktree is clean and the head read 1418d875ea1710a6f7f51613c07b3379642514a3 from git rev-parse before and after.\n\nNOT DONE, deliberately. No documentation change: nothing in docs/ states behaviour this makes false, and the conditions did not ask for one. Reading the vocabulary costs one projection of the log on the direct CLI path, which a chain of writes in one process pays for once.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:b2bbee486f27c45671ebf3fad0898cd97cd6f604","branch":"request/undefined-kind-warning","head":"1418d875ea1710a6f7f51613c07b3379642514a3","status":"ready-for-review","tests":"vet,test,race,gofmt,2-reverted-half-mutations"}}